// Typechecking covers MORE than the build does. `tsconfig.json` compiles `src/`
// alone (it has to: `rootDir` is src, and `dist/` must mirror it), so everything
// outside src — the tests, the eval harness, the import scripts — was checked by
// no gate at all: a test could reference a function that no longer exists and
// nothing would say so until someone ran it.
//
// Bringing `test/` under this surfaced 29 gaps, almost all the same shape: a
// value read out of an array or a counter map, used without ever establishing
// that it exists. `const [w] = parse(...)` followed by `assert.equal(w.type,
// 'run')` does fail if the parse returned nothing — but it fails as a TypeError
// on a line that looks like an assertion, which reads as a broken test rather
// than a broken parser. Those reads now carry an explicit `assert.ok`, so the
// precondition the test always assumed is stated and reported as itself.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "eval/**/*.ts", "scripts/**/*.ts", "test/**/*.ts"]
}
